I am not certain now I have a full backup of that bucket given such behaviors, and it remains unclear what caused it. 

I think if git-annex at least provided more info -- which key and which versionId were "not available" -- it might have helped to shine the light... I guess there might be some form of interaction with our "trailing delete" policy where older versions get removed but it is unlikely there is a race condition this fast.

bucket `dandiarchive` is versioned and most of the files are openly available there

```
(venv-10.20261102) dandi@drogon:/mnt/backup/dandi/dandiset-manifests$ git show git-annex:remote.log
09b87154-c650-46d1-a036-6e03c56c0b1a bucket=dandiarchive datacenter=US encryption=none fileprefix=dandisets/ host=s3.amazonaws.com importtree=yes name=s3-dandiarchive port=80 publicurl=https://dandiarchive.s3.amazonaws.com/ region=us-east-2 signature=v4 storageclass=STANDARD type=S3 timestamp=1764702488s
```

and this particular "folder" seems to be  accessible, e.g. since can browse/see on [quilt data](https://app.quilt.bio/b/dandiarchive/tree/dandisets/001412/draft/)

the "problem" is (yet to report/have it addressed) is that we keep rewriting those files too fast too often, so e.g. this one has 

```
dandi@drogon:~$ aws s3api list-object-versions     --bucket dandiarchive     --prefix dandisets/001412/draft/assets.yaml     --query "Versions[].{VersionId: VersionId, LastModified: LastModified}"     --output table | wc -l 
1086

dandi@drogon:~$ aws s3api list-object-versions     --bucket dandiarchive     --prefix dandisets/001412/draft/assets.yaml     --query "Versions[].{VersionId: VersionId, LastModified: LastModified}"     --output table | head -n 6
-------------------------------------------------------------------
|                       ListObjectVersions                        |
+----------------------------+------------------------------------+
|        LastModified        |             VersionId              |
+----------------------------+------------------------------------+
|  2026-11-03T16:40:06+00:00 |  pBuWBb3vXNGKn5kW_40eWg05mWg1k_IQ  |
dandi@drogon:~$ aws s3api list-object-versions     --bucket dandiarchive     --prefix dandisets/001412/draft/assets.yaml     --query "Versions[].{VersionId: VersionId, LastModified: LastModified}"     --output table | tail -n 3
|  2026-11-02T00:00:51+00:00 |  yyNkMORu2sgOxjeMq7k29Onj_Jw1MB13  |
|  2026-11-01T23:59:50+00:00 |  rw5Oxaff7g_fK5rF17Gi7Mfv.x1pLsp5  |
+----------------------------+------------------------------------+
```

but they are all there and should be accessible so I am not sure why git-annex errors out. Indeed a new version of the key might arrive while annex is importing a prior one (might want even to gate versions may be given a timestamp?), but that IMHO warrants a warning (since it still managed to import) not an error.


